<text id="02-output-contract" title="rust-tokio-async Output Contract" version="1.1.0" est_tokens="900" depth="essential">
  <summary>JSON Schema (draft-07) for the code artefact this methodology produces, with valid and invalid examples and forbidden patterns.</summary>

  <section title="Schema">
    <code lang="json"><![CDATA[
{
  "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
  "$id": "https://faion.net/schemas/rust-tokio-async.json",
  "type": "object",
  "required": [
    "pattern",
    "concurrency_bound",
    "all_io_timed_out",
    "no_lock_across_await"
  ],
  "properties": {
    "pattern": {
      "enum": [
        "try_join",
        "spawn_blocking",
        "buffer_unordered_semaphore",
        "join_set",
        "select"
      ]
    },
    "concurrency_bound": {
      "type": "integer",
      "minimum": 1
    },
    "all_io_timed_out": {
      "const": true
    },
    "no_lock_across_await": {
      "const": true
    },
    "uses_join_set_for_dynamic": {
      "type": "boolean"
    },
    "select_branches_documented": {
      "type": "boolean"
    }
  }
}
]]></code>
  </section>

  <example valid="true">
    <code lang="json"><![CDATA[
{
  "pattern": "buffer_unordered_semaphore",
  "concurrency_bound": 16,
  "all_io_timed_out": true,
  "no_lock_across_await": true,
  "uses_join_set_for_dynamic": true,
  "select_branches_documented": true
}
]]></code>
  </example>

  <example valid="false">
    <code lang="json"><![CDATA[
{
  "pattern": "try_join",
  "concurrency_bound": 10000,
  "all_io_timed_out": false,
  "no_lock_across_await": false,
  "uses_join_set_for_dynamic": false,
  "select_branches_documented": false
}
]]></code>
    <note>try_join over 10000 futures (use buffer_unordered); missing timeouts; lock across .await.</note>
  </example>

  <section title="Runtime-level companion contract">
    <p>The schema above is PER-PATTERN — it pins one concurrency decision. The service also owes ONE runtime-level record, fixed once and reviewed with the same rigour. Both must be present; the per-pattern record is meaningless on a misconfigured runtime.</p>
    <code lang="json"><![CDATA[
{
  "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
  "$id": "https://faion.net/schemas/rust-tokio-runtime.json",
  "type": "object",
  "required": [
    "runtime_flavour",
    "worker_threads",
    "blocking_offload",
    "channel_policy",
    "timeout_default_ms"
  ],
  "properties": {
    "runtime_flavour": {"type": "string", "enum": ["multi_thread", "current_thread"]},
    "worker_threads": {"type": "integer", "minimum": 1},
    "blocking_offload": {"type": "string", "enum": ["spawn_blocking", "rayon", "none"]},
    "channel_policy": {
      "type": "object",
      "required": ["bounded", "default_capacity"]
    },
    "timeout_default_ms": {"type": "integer", "minimum": 1},
    "shutdown_signal": {"type": "string"}
  }
}
]]></code>
    <example valid="true">
      <code lang="json"><![CDATA[
{
  "runtime_flavour": "multi_thread",
  "worker_threads": 8,
  "blocking_offload": "spawn_blocking",
  "channel_policy": {"bounded": true, "default_capacity": 1024},
  "timeout_default_ms": 3000,
  "shutdown_signal": "ctrl_c+CancellationToken"
}
]]></code>
    </example>
    <example valid="false">
      <code lang="json"><![CDATA[
{
  "runtime_flavour": "default",
  "worker_threads": 0,
  "blocking_offload": "inline",
  "channel_policy": {"bounded": false},
  "timeout_default_ms": 0
}
]]></code>
      <note>runtime_flavour not in enum; worker_threads &lt; 1; blocking_offload=inline is forbidden; channel_policy missing default_capacity; timeout_default_ms &lt; 1.</note>
    </example>
    <reference path="templates/runtime-spec-example.json">Filled-in runtime-level record.</reference>
  </section>

  <section title="Forbidden">
    <forbidden id="f1">try_join! over a Vec/iterator with unknown or large N.</forbidden>
    <forbidden id="f2">I/O call without tokio::time::timeout.</forbidden>
    <forbidden id="f3">std::sync::MutexGuard alive across an .await point.</forbidden>
    <forbidden id="f4">Vec&lt;JoinHandle&lt;T&gt;&gt; instead of JoinSet for dynamic task groups.</forbidden>
    <forbidden id="f5">spawn_blocking awaited with .await? (missing the second ? for join error).</forbidden>
    <forbidden id="f6">Blocking syscall on an async path: std::fs, std::thread::sleep, blocking sync mutex, CPU loop over ~1ms.</forbidden>
    <forbidden id="f7">mpsc::unbounded_channel on a production path.</forbidden>
    <forbidden id="f8">tokio::spawn whose JoinHandle is dropped — the task leaks and its panic is swallowed.</forbidden>
    <forbidden id="f9">Default runtime build in production (no explicit flavour, no worker_threads).</forbidden>
  </section>

  <reference path="scripts/validate-rust-tokio-async.py">Validator script.</reference>
</text>
